---
import InnerTitle from "~/components/widgets/InnerTitle.astro";
import Layout from "~/layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const metadata = {
	title: "BCH Governance and Upgrades",
	description:
		"How Bitcoin Cash changes: the CHIP process, yearly May 15 upgrades from CashTokens to loops and functions, and the open debate over faster blocks for 2027.",
};
---

<Layout {metadata}>
  <!-- InnerTitle Widget ******************* -->

  <InnerTitle>
    <Fragment slot="title">Bitcoin Cash Governance</Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="subtitle">No foundation, no treasury, no CEO. Proposals, public debate and one upgrade every May 15.</Fragment>
  </InnerTitle>

  <div
    class="mx-auto px-6 sm:px-6 max-w-3xl prose prose-lg lg:prose-xl mt-8 mb-8"
  >
    <p>
      Bitcoin Cash has no foundation, no treasury and no company in charge. A change ships only when node teams, wallets,
      exchanges, miners and app builders agree to run it. Nobody can force an upgrade, and nobody can block one alone.
    </p>

    <p>
      The result is slow on purpose. It is also predictable: the network upgrades once a year, on May 15, and each upgrade
      is locked in about six months ahead.
    </p>

    <div class="aspect-video w-full max-w-[900px]">
      <iframe
        class="w-full h-full"
        src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/lQTmDjlYviE"
        title="YouTube video player"
        style="border: 0;"
        allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
        allowfullscreen></iframe>
    </div>

    <h3>How a change happens: CHIPs</h3>

    <p>
      A change starts as a <a href="https://gitlab.com/im_uname/cash-improvement-proposals/-/blob/master/CHIPs.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Cash Improvement Proposal (CHIP)</a
      >. The author publishes a specification, answers objections and collects statements from stakeholders: node teams,
      wallets, exchanges, miners and app developers.
    </p>

    <p>
      Debate happens in public at <a href="https://bitcoincashresearch.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >BitcoinCashResearch.org</a
      >. If the proposal wins broad support, node software ships it with an activation date. The test network (chipnet)
      activates it about six months before mainnet.
    </p>

    <h3>Recent upgrades</h3>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>May 15</th><th>What changed</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>2023</td><td>CashTokens: native fungible tokens and NFTs inside the coin itself.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2024</td><td>ABLA: the block size limit adapts to sustained demand, from a 32 MB floor.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2025</td><td>VM limits and BigInt: a density-based compute budget and arbitrary-precision math for contracts.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2026</td><td>Loops, functions, bitwise ops and pay-to-script outputs, plus 128-byte NFT commitments.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Under discussion for 2027</h3>

    <p>
      The main proposal is <strong>Faster Blocks</strong>: cut the average block time from 10 minutes to 1 minute. Supporters
      want quicker confirmations. Critics worry about orphan rates, light-wallet impact and exchange coordination. It is
      not decided. The lock-in decision for a May 2027 activation falls around November 15, 2026.
    </p>

    <h3>The trade-off</h3>

    <p>
      Without a treasury, most development runs on volunteers and crowdfunding such as Flipstarter. That keeps any single
      group from capturing the chain. It also means progress depends on people choosing to show up and fund the work.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
